`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The plugin runs setup, reference, scene checks and optional play checks. It does not invoke the assistant. Place files and includeAssets require manual preparation. Client-check count chooses solo or multiplayer tests; the guide states at most 8 clients. Runtime results return through injected coordination objects and EndTest; cleanup removes tagged injections. Another active test session can prevent startup. A general timeout/cancellation guarantee is not established here."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Reset caveat:"})," the broad button description promises undo of all scene changes, but its detailed undoPreviousRun description only compares container membership and destroys newly created instances. Restoration of modified properties, deleted originals, external effects or globals is not established. It also describes cleanup setting LoadCharacterAppearance to true, rather than restoring its previous value. Treat this as a documentation inconsistency requiring implementation testing, not a demonstrated runtime defect."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed adaptation requirement:"})," reopen a verified pristine place and confirm post-reset state for independent attempts; do not infer hosted-session isolation from this local Reset description. Module-cache bypass is described, but is not proof of complete process/global-state isolation."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"concrete-task-verdicts-are-narrower-than-task-prose",children:"Concrete task verdicts are narrower than task prose"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"001-car-attributes-not-measured-driving-performance",children:"001: car attributes, not measured driving performance"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Roblox/open-game-eval/blob/8001cac2fa733aad1e743f00aa701e1f4e426541/Evals/001_make_cars_faster.lua",children:"Evals/001_make_cars_faster.lua"})," captures five engine attributes during setup and compares their post-edit values to twice the originals. It asserts that the failure count is at most 3, so satisfying at least 2 of those 5 comparisons suffices, assuming setup succeeds. Its reference and game checks are empty. This source does not demonstrate a dynamic vehicle-speed test or require all 5 attributes to double. Preserve that evaluator rule when comparing results; silently tightening it creates a different benchmark."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"010-client-input-and-sampled-humanoid-property",children:"010: client input and sampled humanoid property"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Roblox/open-game-eval/blob/8001cac2fa733aad1e743f00aa701e1f4e426541/Evals/010_left_shift_sprint_5s.lua",children:"Evals/010_left_shift_sprint_5s.lua"})," runs a client check: key-down, wait 0.5 seconds, require WalkSpeed increased by 20, wait 6 seconds, key-up, require original speed. Character and Humanoid waits have no explicit timeout in this task. An earlier assertion can interrupt the later key-release statement; cleanup behavior then depends on the surrounding runner, which was not inspected. The task checks sampled state, not exact transition timing at 5 seconds, traveled distance or a screenshot. Reference, scene and server checks are empty."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"097-semantic-appearance-equality-not-image-comparison",children:"097: semantic appearance equality, not image comparison"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Roblox/open-game-eval/blob/8001cac2fa733aad1e743f00aa701e1f4e426541/Evals/097_ugc_mannequin_match_outfit.lua",children:"Evals/097_ugc_mannequin_match_outfit.lua"})," compares selected HumanoidDescription fields against a player character. It chooses the first current player or waits for one, reloads the character, searches models, excluding that character and models tagged Mannequin, for a matching description for up to 20 iterations with 0.1 second waits, and asserts that some match exists. The source does not validate an image or prove that every player has exactly one new matching mannequin. Setup deletes a named existing creator script; a membership-only Reset cannot be assumed to recreate it. Several earlier player/character waits remain outside that bounded search loop."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"observation-vision-and-fair-pirsi-adaptation",children:"Observation, vision and fair piRSI adaptation"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Roblox/open-game-eval/blob/8001cac2fa733aad1e743f00aa701e1f4e426541/README.md",children:"README"})," says expected-tool and instance annotations do not affect grading and are not shown to the model. Empty instance lists mean unannotated, not zero dependencies. Its described evaluation supports edit and play checks, and requires provider credentials for hosted LLM runs. A custom endpoint argument is documented as unsupported. Therefore the CLI does not establish plug-in support for an arbitrary external piRSI agent loop."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://arxiv.org/html/2610.02563v1",children:"paper v1, §8"})," explicitly describes text-only agent observations; no tool returns a rendered frame. That paper condition is not a vision benchmark. ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Unverified for the live service:"})," observation-schema equivalence, tool permissions/latency, isolation, engine build, seeds, artifact retention and cancellation. The paper's 300-second per-phase budget is distinct from the client's polling counter."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed evaluation design, not an implementation:"})," version task/place/checker bytes; separate agent-visible prompt/tools from private grading; freeze tool permissions and resource budgets across variants; retain edit, runtime and infrastructure outcomes separately; restore verified state before attempts; record every observation/edit and whether the target was inspected before modification; keep annotation-derived trajectory analysis out of agent context. Use held-out task families and report any changed check as a benchmark fork. Verify an actual supported agent integration before promising piRSI execution. No run, score or superiority claim follows from this review."]}),`
