`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/waynchi/gamedevbench/blob/39952ba6341898380ff1c2c3336101c57c99196b/README.md",children:"inspected README at 39952ba6341898380ff1c2c3336101c57c99196b"})," describes 333 tasks, exact Godot 4.4.1, public task/ground-truth archives and runner/validation code. A newer Godot override is experimental, not leaderboard-comparable. Linux screenshot/video execution requires a display path, normally Xvfb; windowless operation is not an excuse to omit graphics tasks. Strict confinement is documented as the default: filtered writable task workspace, no ground truths/prior results/sibling workspaces, per-solver display isolation, restricted provider egress and fresh credential-free validation. Unconfined runs are diagnostic. Resume retains earlier results outside the selected rerun set, so a resumed aggregate may not describe only newly attempted tasks. These are inspected documentation claims, not an independent sandbox or benchmark audit. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/waynchi/gamedevbench/blob/39952ba6341898380ff1c2c3336101c57c99196b/LICENSE",children:"same-revision LICENSE"})," is Apache-2.0; per-task assets and upstream content still require their own inventory. Public reference solutions make access control and contamination disclosure important even when tasks are packaged to reduce accidental exposure."]}),`
