`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Public test material may already be present in a base model's training data. Isolation can reduce experiment-time leakage but cannot prove absence of prior contamination. A held-out partition should group related projects, tutorial derivatives and nearly identical tasks rather than merely randomizing filenames. If public task coverage is too small, report the limitation rather than call the result general self-improvement."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"proposed-evaluation-record",children:"Proposed evaluation record"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Freeze task identifiers and origin groups; content/asset hashes; evaluator and engine versions; solver model and reasoning settings; candidate harness revision; allowed API/GUI/file surfaces; training/selection/test membership; memory provenance; model-token/tool-call/time budgets; seed and fresh-start policy; build and runtime logs; screenshots/video and authoritative checks; final judge configuration; raw terminal outcomes and resource costs. Preserve credential references only, never secrets. Do not configure any credential transmission merely to fill this record."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"For each candidate, retain paired baseline/candidate outcomes on the same tasks and report the sampling unit. Separate valid task failures from harness/infrastructure failures and give denominator policy before viewing results. Repeat stochastic runs where justified; a single successful retry is not a robust capability. Run the final held-out evaluation only after selection, and archive the unsuccessful candidates too. None of these fixtures, statistical comparisons or execution permissions has been established by this source-only review."}),`
