`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Checked 2026-10-18. Read-only source inspection at ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"f1cfdee2856e9dc4b5b4dc5cc2e391d0aa20d819"}),", the revision already used for the adapter review. No external code, models or evaluations were run. These are code-level boundaries and proposed tests, not reproduced overspending or game-performance findings. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/gepa-ai/gepa/blob/f1cfdee2856e9dc4b5b4dc5cc2e391d0aa20d819/LICENSE",children:"MIT license"})," does not supply model-service or asset rights."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"count-proposal-tasks-separately-from-iterations-and-retained-candidates",children:"Count proposal tasks separately from iterations and retained candidates"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/gepa-ai/gepa/blob/f1cfdee2856e9dc4b5b4dc5cc2e391d0aa20d819/src/gepa/strategies/proposal_sampling.py",children:"sampling strategies"})," can produce one, N or P×N parent/minibatch tasks per iteration. However, ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/gepa-ai/gepa/blob/f1cfdee2856e9dc4b5b4dc5cc2e391d0aa20d819/src/gepa/utils/stop_condition.py",children:"MaxCandidateProposalsStopper"})," checks ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"state.i"}),", which the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/gepa-ai/gepa/blob/f1cfdee2856e9dc4b5b4dc5cc2e391d0aa20d819/src/gepa/core/engine.py",children:"main loop"})," increments once per iteration. Equal settings therefore do not guarantee equal actual proposal counts. ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"MaxTrackedCandidatesStopper"})," counts the retained candidate pool, not all failed, skipped or discarded proposals. This does not imply every sampled task produces a new candidate. Parent selection is called repeatedly without a distinct-parent constraint in these samplers; the strategy name alone does not establish unique parents."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed GameMap control:"})," retain separate iteration, proposal-task, generated-proposal, unique-candidate, admitted-candidate, actual-evaluation and cache-hit counts. Match actual search resources when comparing broader sampling against a better selector, and preserve costs for discarded branches."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"a-stop-condition-is-not-hard-admission-control-or-remote-cancellation",children:"A stop condition is not hard admission control or remote cancellation"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/gepa-ai/gepa/blob/f1cfdee2856e9dc4b5b4dc5cc2e391d0aa20d819/src/gepa/utils/stop_condition.py",children:"MaxMetricCallsStopper"})," compares accumulated evaluation count. On a fresh run, ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/gepa-ai/gepa/blob/f1cfdee2856e9dc4b5b4dc5cc2e391d0aa20d819/src/gepa/core/engine.py",children:"engine.run"})," evaluates the seed on the validation batch before reaching the main loop's stop check. This static path does not guarantee rejecting an over-budget initial batch before execution. The loop-boundary check does not itself cancel an in-flight model, renderer or evaluator. ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"TimeoutStopCondition"})," starts its clock at object construction, not automatically at remote-job submission."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["There is a concrete cost-tracking caveat: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/gepa-ai/gepa/blob/f1cfdee2856e9dc4b5b4dc5cc2e391d0aa20d819/src/gepa/api.py",children:"optimize"})," wraps an ordinary ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"reflection_lm"})," callable lacking ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"total_cost"})," in ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/gepa-ai/gepa/blob/f1cfdee2856e9dc4b5b4dc5cc2e391d0aa20d819/src/gepa/lm.py",children:"TrackingLM"}),". That wrapper estimates tokens but reports cost ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"0.0"}),"; a positive ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"max_reflection_cost"})," alone cannot trip on that path. The separate custom ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"reflection_strategy"})," path has additional cost-capability checks and must not be conflated with it. Even supported reflection-cost accounting does not automatically include task-model, renderer, tool or human costs."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed GameMap control:"})," reserve a bounded batch budget before dispatch; independently enforce call, rendering and wall-time limits; record in-flight work and final reconciliation. Probe whether cost measurement is supported rather than interpreting zero as free. Verify executor/service cancellation separately. Use a no-external-call mock adapter for limit tests, not a live paid endpoint."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"cache-hits-and-resume-are-not-independent-repetitions",children:"Cache hits and resume are not independent repetitions"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/gepa-ai/gepa/blob/f1cfdee2856e9dc4b5b4dc5cc2e391d0aa20d819/src/gepa/core/state.py",children:"EvaluationCache"})," keys contain a candidate-text hash, train/val namespace and example ID. Distinct train/val loaders already have separate namespaces; the same loader deliberately shares one. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/gepa-ai/gepa/blob/f1cfdee2856e9dc4b5b4dc5cc2e391d0aa20d819/src/gepa/core/data_loader.py",children:"ListDataLoader"})," uses positions as IDs, not content hashes. The key has no independent model, engine, evaluator, asset, environment or trial identity fields; callers must encode or invalidate those changes themselves."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/gepa-ai/gepa/blob/f1cfdee2856e9dc4b5b4dc5cc2e391d0aa20d819/src/gepa/api.py",children:"API contract"})," and ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/gepa-ai/gepa/blob/f1cfdee2856e9dc4b5b4dc5cc2e391d0aa20d819/src/gepa/core/engine.py",children:"engine"})," reuse the saved seed's validation evidence when ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"gepa_state.bin"})," exists; an identical supplied seed already in the pool causes no extra seed evaluation. A supplied seed absent from that pool is instead evaluated and added before the main stop check, also advancing ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"state.i"}),". Migration discards old unnamespaced cache entries but leaves previously recorded validation scores intact. Disabling evaluation caching does not itself erase those candidate scores or start a fresh experiment. Additionally, the engine's full-validation path bypasses cache when ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"write_agent_state"})," is enabled so it can capture trajectories: richer recording is not necessarily cost-neutral."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed GameMap control:"})," bind data contents/order, model/engine/adapter/evaluator versions, assets and reset policy into an experiment fingerprint. Use a fresh run directory for semantic changes rather than reusing saved scoring state. For independent stochastic trials, use fresh state or explicit trial-aware identities; returning the same cached observation does not add a sample. Record trace/cache settings and distinguish cumulative resumed results from newly executed work. GEPA's valset is used for selection and defaults to trainset when omitted; keep final assessment outside optimization rather than treating that parameter name as a protected test split."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Unimplemented acceptance fixtures:"})," zero remaining budget with a larger initial validation batch; actual task/proposal counts under N and P×N sampling; a callable without real cost tracking; rejection of incompatible resume after dataset reordering or evaluator changes; actual evaluation counts with cache/trace settings toggled; and independent repeats of the same candidate. None was executed, and no general vulnerability or capability gain is asserted."]}),`
