`,e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Choose what time means."})," The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/cfe490d941f992655948eee8fd4fd94e1c4234bf/docs/src/api/class-clock.md",children:"Clock API"})," distinguishes ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"setFixedTime"})," (fixed Date values while timers continue), ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"setSystemTime"})," (change wall time without firing timers), ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"runFor"})," (advance through callbacks), and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"fastForward"}),"/",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"pauseAt"})," (jump, firing overdue timers at most once). Thus replacing a five-second gameplay interval with a five-second jump can change how many update callbacks run. That consequence is GameMap's application to game tests, not a measured game defect."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"The animation cadence is synthetic."})," ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/cfe490d941f992655948eee8fd4fd94e1c4234bf/packages/injected/src/clock.ts#L355-L401",children:"Injected source"})," supplies animation callbacks with simulated ticks and schedules each new frame request for the next 16 ms boundary; the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/cfe490d941f992655948eee8fd4fd94e1c4234bf/tests/library/unit/clock.spec.ts#L1283-L1359",children:"unit tests"})," assert this grid. A jump can instead deliver an already-overdue frame at its destination, because the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/cfe490d941f992655948eee8fd4fd94e1c4234bf/packages/injected/src/clock.ts#L277-L291",children:"jump path"})," reschedules overdue timers there. This is not measured display refresh, GPU throughput or evidence that the game uses a 60 Hz physics step. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/cfe490d941f992655948eee8fd4fd94e1c4234bf/packages/injected/src/clock.ts#L294-L323",children:"Timer creation"})," schedules a zero-delay timer created during a tick one millisecond later. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/cfe490d941f992655948eee8fd4fd94e1c4234bf/tests/library/page-clock.spec.ts#L473-L519",children:"Tests"})," show that such a nested callback at the requested endpoint needs another advance, including when scheduled through a microtask."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Installation and isolation are explicit inputs."})," The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/cfe490d941f992655948eee8fd4fd94e1c4234bf/docs/src/clock.md#L24-L44",children:"guide"})," warns that installation must precede use of the replaced timer APIs. The API's scope is the entire browser context, including its pages and iframes, not one isolated page. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/cfe490d941f992655948eee8fd4fd94e1c4234bf/packages/playwright-core/src/server/clock.ts#L37-L110",children:"Server dispatch"})," applies clock operations to frames and preserves initialization instructions for later documents. Do not treat sibling pages as independent time-controlled trials or infer worker, Web Audio, network/server or whole-browser synchronization from that scope."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Manual advance is not an instantaneous, atomic step."})," ",e.jsxs(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/cfe490d941f992655948eee8fd4fd94e1c4234bf/packages/injected/src/clock.ts#L169-L195",children:[e.jsx(t.code,{children:"runFor"})," and its timer loop"]})," continue processing due timers after catching a synchronous callback Error, advance the clock, then rethrow the first Error. A ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/cfe490d941f992655948eee8fd4fd94e1c4234bf/tests/library/page-clock.spec.ts#L98-L104",children:"browser test"})," expects a later callback to run before rejection. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/cfe490d941f992655948eee8fd4fd94e1c4234bf/packages/injected/src/clock.ts#L355-L393",children:"callback invoker"})," yields through a real timer after each callback and does not await a callback's returned promise. A rejected advance therefore does not imply unchanged state or safe retry; its completion is not a network/asset-readiness barrier."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Keep performance measurement outside this treatment."})," The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/cfe490d941f992655948eee8fd4fd94e1c4234bf/packages/injected/src/clock.ts#L754-L772",children:"performance replacement"})," makes ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"performance.now()"})," follow simulated ticks. For the performance methods copied by this implementation, entry queries return empty arrays and mark/measure calls return synthetic entries. These readings cannot substantiate native frame-time or resource-timing claims. Separate real-clock performance runs from virtual-time functional runs."]}),`
`]}),`
