`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Record game/build hash, Playwright and actual browser revision, context identity, initialization/readiness policy, clock mode, starting wall/monotonic values, ordered clock commands and input events, randomness/reset policy, application tick counters, callback/error trace and post-step state. The release's ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/cfe490d941f992655948eee8fd4fd94e1c4234bf/packages/playwright-core/browsers.json",children:"browser inventory"})," is an expected dependency list, not proof of the installed executable."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Use an explicitly quiescent game-start boundary after bootstrap; a large ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"pauseAt"})," jump during active gameplay is itself a suspension treatment. Confirm the starting state before issuing player input. Keep real-clock play, fully stepped virtual time and suspend/resume probes as distinct conditions with separately declared oracles. Require an application-owned completion signal for asynchronous effects rather than adding arbitrary extra simulated time until a test passes."]}),`
