`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://arxiv.org/html/2609.00069v1",children:"Auditing Harness Tampering in Self-Improving Agents, v1"})," adds a change-level perspective: obligations can fail during execution, evaluation, selection, recording or propagation. Its constructed dataset inserts matched faulty/benign edits into recorded changes; classification receives target lines, while localization must find them. Construction supplies labels and human inspection covers a subset. The reported natural-run analysis applies a model auditor to released trajectories. Its finding rates are not independently established defect prevalence, and seeded-control false-positive rates do not establish natural-run precision. An ancestor's flagged edit does not prove activation or a causal score gain in its descendants. The reviewed paper/deposited manuscript archive did not establish an author-linked auditor, labeled-data or full-output release; availability remains unverified. Paper licensing does not establish software/data rights. No auditor or alleged defect was executed here."]}),`
