`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://arxiv.org/html/2606.17861v1",children:"GameCraft-Bench"})," evaluates complete Godot projects and agent-supplied demonstrations. At upstream ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench/tree/a43347534374df9a0c1a6c001aa9380862783f6d",children:e.jsx(t.code,{children:"a4334753"})}),", shared by the later adapters, traces remain development-visible; “hidden” describes the evaluation rubric's role, not secret test trajectories. Named scenarios may initialize advanced states. Credit therefore concerns demonstrated requirements, not independently discovered playability or enjoyment. This source audit ran no games or judges."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Evidence budget."})," The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench/blob/a43347534374df9a0c1a6c001aa9380862783f6d/tasks/cardgame-autobattler/instruction.md#L98-L152",children:"task contract"})," asks for 1–10 traces, capped at 600 frames at 30 FPS. With overridable defaults, the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench/blob/a43347534374df9a0c1a6c001aa9380862783f6d/gamecraft_bench/verifier/score.py#L110-L184",children:"scorer"})," keeps the first ten filenames before replay. Each ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench/blob/a43347534374df9a0c1a6c001aa9380862783f6d/gamecraft_bench/verifier/replay.py#L73-L218",children:"fresh launch"})," defaults to a 1280×720 input viewport and resized 854×480 MP4. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench/blob/a43347534374df9a0c1a6c001aa9380862783f6d/gamecraft_bench/verifier/score.py#L342-L402",children:"frame sampler"})," defaults to 0.5-second spacing and, for longer recordings, a contiguous 20-second window seeded by demo name; a short recording can have its final frame cloned. Replay separately defaults to a 90-second limit. These are distinct submission, replay and observation limits."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench/blob/a43347534374df9a0c1a6c001aa9380862783f6d/gamecraft_bench/verifier/judges/openai_gpt.py#L59-L139",children:"OpenAI judge"}),", defaulting to GPT-5.5, sends at most 40 sampled PNGs, as do the released Claude/Kimi paths. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench/blob/a43347534374df9a0c1a6c001aa9380862783f6d/gamecraft_bench/verifier/judges/gemini.py#L39-L100",children:"Gemini path"})," sends the full MP4 instead. The sampling window is not a universal video-duration cap; provider choice can change evidence modality as well as judgment."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Aggregation and failures."})," Each ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench/blob/a43347534374df9a0c1a6c001aa9380862783f6d/gamecraft_bench/verifier/score.py#L298-L317",children:"rubric item"})," uses max (default) or mean across scored demos; different items can win on different playthroughs. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench/blob/a43347534374df9a0c1a6c001aa9380862783f6d/tasks/cardgame-autobattler/tests/rubric.json#L1-L9",children:"inspected task rubric"})," combines item averages with a build gate and mechanics/depth/visuals/art weights of 15/35/15/35. A caught replay failure is logged and skipped, shrinking a mean's demo denominator. By contrast, five failed judge attempts produce item zeros for that replayed demo. Missing, null or non-numeric answers, including “NA,” also become zero; there is no coverage-exclusion rule. No successful evidence leaves requirements at zero. Preserve failure counts alongside scores. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench/blob/a43347534374df9a0c1a6c001aa9380862783f6d/gamecraft_bench/verifier/score.py#L142-L268",children:"Failure handling"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench/blob/a43347534374df9a0c1a6c001aa9380862783f6d/gamecraft_bench/verifier/judges/_common.py#L68-L106",children:"response parser"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Release and transfer."})," The pin contains 140 task packages plus an example, public rubrics, evaluator and reference-source material; some reference scripts are ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench/blob/a43347534374df9a0c1a6c001aa9380862783f6d/tasks/sports-archery-quest/solution/solve.sh",children:"placeholders"}),". This is not an inspected all-task run archive. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench/blob/a43347534374df9a0c1a6c001aa9380862783f6d/LICENSE",children:"Apache-2.0"})," covers repository code; downloaded asset entries retain their own terms. For a proposed GameMap comparison, freeze project/trace hashes, filenames, scenarios, capture/sampling settings, backend/model and failure denominator. Keep upstream replay, RSIGame's patched/padded replay and Recursive Game Creator's native recordings separately labelled even when they share a rubric and formula."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"rsigame-persistent-evidence-and-retained-game-checkpoints",children:"RSIGame: persistent evidence and retained game checkpoints"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://arxiv.org/html/2609.39045v1",children:"RSIGame v1"})," combines evidence-directed game editing, an evolving checklist and separate checkpoint selection; optional guidance starts another stage. Training-free rounds change game artifacts and working context, while separate experience internalization fine-tunes the generator. Neither demonstrates recursive harness-code optimization. The benchmark rubric is hidden, but submission demos remain visible during development. A small free-play check changes interaction paths on existing tasks; it does not establish unseen-game or human-enjoyment generalization."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Source-inspected mechanism."})," At ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/WenyiWU0111/RSIGame/tree/1214b342fce22e97fe19bfc56be189d06f44634b",children:"commit 1214b342"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/WenyiWU0111/RSIGame/blob/1214b342fce22e97fe19bfc56be189d06f44634b/src/rsigame/checklist/checklist_state.py",children:"checklist state"})," retains supported findings when a later replay does not observe an item, while tracking staleness and deferral separately. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/WenyiWU0111/RSIGame/blob/1214b342fce22e97fe19bfc56be189d06f44634b/src/rsigame/controller/verify.py",children:"issue verifier"})," combines observed persistence/disappearance/non-exercise with the editor's attempted-work report, preserving partial fixes and unknowns. These are model-assisted runtime observations, not authoritative behavioral assertions. Champion selection ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/WenyiWU0111/RSIGame/blob/1214b342fce22e97fe19bfc56be189d06f44634b/src/rsigame/eval/estimator/aggregate.py",children:"compares criterion values on common observed coverage"}),"; an unobserved criterion is excluded rather than scored zero."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Stopping and scoring."})," The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/WenyiWU0111/RSIGame/blob/1214b342fce22e97fe19bfc56be189d06f44634b/src/rsigame/monitor/live.py#L14-L34",children:"released default"})," retrospectively selects checkpoints after all 30 development rounds, explicitly identified as the paper-run procedure. Retrospective stopping estimates should not be presented as prospectively avoided calls. Optional live monitoring ends at a round boundary and does not roll the working tree back. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/WenyiWU0111/RSIGame/blob/1214b342fce22e97fe19bfc56be189d06f44634b/src/rsigame/eval/score_game.py",children:"scoring wrapper"})," conditionally extends replay duration beyond the benchmark's original cap and records that deviation. Preserve the exact replay/padding configuration and selected build."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Release and rights."})," The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/datasets/RSIGame/RSIGame-TableArtifacts/tree/2735939d5a75c95c6cb67130a9485fbc0e3881cc",children:"pinned HF release"})," lists base/scored game archives, judge records and 19 manifests; intermediate rounds and full recordings are excluded. Source-only arithmetic reproduces their 19 advertised rounded means using the full 140-task denominator, including missing-task zeros. This does not recompute gameplay scores. Five of the current paper's 24 main-result rows are absent from this inspected release. No dataset license is declared in the inspected card/root. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/WenyiWU0111/RSIGame/blob/1214b342fce22e97fe19bfc56be189d06f44634b/LICENSE",children:"Code Apache-2.0"})," does not establish rights to game assets, model weights or external services. The required repair fork and patched GameCraft dependency need separate pins; this code revision is not established as the experimental commit."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed transfer, unimplemented:"})," compare last-build return, fixed-budget champion selection and prospective live stopping on an owned fixture containing a regression, an unexercised feature and a failed judge. Keep game-edit search distinct from harness search. No model, engine, benchmark or released test was run here."]}),`
